model leg_on_row
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.2 G1 S-6 (#211, plan §4): an observed row's leg has no day of its own either, so a row whose leg states an on (a date, not a window) is refused by the grammar (LOAD-PARSE at the row's line, before its closing parenthesis). On a statement the later cash is its own row; the twin cut_leg_on_row_twin is the same row on the cash's own day."

source bank "bank"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input bank_rows: observed
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place unexplained: outside lives 1900-01-01..

version stmt
  cite bank
  governs 2026-02
  known 2026-03-02
  covers konto
  pad konto from unexplained
  opening[konto] = 5 000.00 PLN at 2026-02-01 start "wyciąg"
  bank_rows[r1] = (on: 2026-02-03, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 100.00 PLN on 2026-02-05) "line 1"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-02-28)
